        "From a color theory and contrast perspective, flashing cells must adhere strictly to international enterprise standards. In traditional Western financial markets, green indicates price appreciation while red denotes price depreciation. However, in East Asian financial exchanges such as Tokyo and Shanghai, this color convention is precisely inverted: red signifies an upward price rise while green represents a decline. Our enterprise design token architecture abstracts these directional semantics into high-level functional tokens: color-trade-up and color-trade-down, which dynamically resolve to localized palettes based on the user's institutional region configuration.",
